  (18, 91, $seed$Al-Kahf$seed$, $seed$كَذَٰلِكَ وَقَدْ أَحَطْنَا بِمَا لَدَيْهِ خُبْرًۭا$seed$, $seed$Thus. And We had encompassed [all] that he had in knowledge.$seed$),
  (18, 92, $seed$Al-Kahf$seed$, $seed$ثُمَّ أَتْبَعَ سَبَبًا$seed$, $seed$Then he followed a way$seed$),
  (18, 103, $seed$Al-Kahf$seed$, $seed$قُلْ هَلْ نُنَبِّئُكُم بِٱلْأَخْسَرِينَ أَعْمَٰلًا$seed$, $seed$Say, [O Muhammad], "Shall we [believers] inform you of the greatest losers as to [their] deeds?$seed$),
  (18, 108, $seed$Al-Kahf$seed$, $seed$خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَا لَا يَبْغُونَ عَنْهَا حِوَلًۭا$seed$, $seed$Wherein they abide eternally. They will not desire from it any transfer.$seed$),
  (19, 1, $seed$Maryam$seed$, $seed$كٓهيعٓصٓ$seed$, $seed$Kaf, Ha, Ya, 'Ayn, Sad.$seed$),
  (19, 2, $seed$Maryam$seed$, $seed$ذِكْرُ رَحْمَتِ رَبِّكَ عَبْدَهُۥ زَكَرِيَّآ$seed$, $seed$[This is] a mention of the mercy of your Lord to His servant Zechariah$seed$),
  (19, 3, $seed$Maryam$seed$, $seed$إِذْ نَادَىٰ رَبَّهُۥ نِدَآءً خَفِيًّۭا$seed$, $seed$When he called to his Lord a private supplication.$seed$),
  (19, 57, $seed$Maryam$seed$, $seed$وَرَفَعْنَٰهُ مَكَانًا عَلِيًّا$seed$, $seed$And We raised him to a high station.$seed$),
  (19, 80, $seed$Maryam$seed$, $seed$وَنَرِثُهُۥ مَا يَقُولُ وَيَأْتِينَا فَرْدًۭا$seed$, $seed$And We will inherit him [in] what he mentions, and he will come to Us alone.$seed$),
  (19, 86, $seed$Maryam$seed$, $seed$وَنَسُوقُ ٱلْمُجْرِمِينَ إِلَىٰ جَهَنَّمَ وِرْدًۭا$seed$, $seed$And will drive the criminals to Hell in thirst$seed$),
  (19, 88, $seed$Maryam$seed$, $seed$وَقَالُوا۟ ٱتَّخَذَ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنُ وَلَدًۭا$seed$, $seed$And they say, "The Most Merciful has taken [for Himself] a son."$seed$),
  (19, 89, $seed$Maryam$seed$, $seed$لَّقَدْ جِئْتُمْ شَيْـًٔا إِدًّۭا$seed$, $seed$You have done an atrocious thing.$seed$),
  (19, 91, $seed$Maryam$seed$, $seed$أَن دَعَوْا۟ لِلرَّحْمَٰنِ وَلَدًۭا$seed$, $seed$That they attribute to the Most Merciful a son.$seed$),
  (19, 92, $seed$Maryam$seed$, $seed$وَمَا يَنۢبَغِى لِلرَّحْمَٰنِ أَن يَتَّخِذَ وَلَدًا$seed$, $seed$And it is not appropriate for the Most Merciful that He should take a son.$seed$),
  (19, 94, $seed$Maryam$seed$, $seed$لَّقَدْ أَحْصَىٰهُمْ وَعَدَّهُمْ عَدًّۭا$seed$, $seed$He has enumerated them and counted them a [full] counting.$seed$),
  (19, 95, $seed$Maryam$seed$, $seed$وَكُلُّهُمْ ءَاتِيهِ يَوْمَ ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ فَرْدًا$seed$, $seed$And all of them are coming to Him on the Day of Resurrection alone.$seed$),
  (20, 1, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$طه$seed$, $seed$Ta, Ha.$seed$),
  (20, 2, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$مَآ أَنزَلْنَا عَلَيْكَ ٱلْقُرْءَانَ لِتَشْقَىٰٓ$seed$, $seed$We have not sent down to you the Qur'an that you be distressed$seed$),
  (20, 3, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$إِلَّا تَذْكِرَةًۭ لِّمَن يَخْشَىٰ$seed$, $seed$But only as a reminder for those who fear [Allah] -$seed$),
  (20, 5, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$ٱلرَّحْمَٰنُ عَلَى ٱلْعَرْشِ ٱسْتَوَىٰ$seed$, $seed$The Most Merciful [who is] above the Throne established.$seed$),
  (20, 9, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$وَهَلْ أَتَىٰكَ حَدِيثُ مُوسَىٰٓ$seed$, $seed$And has the story of Moses reached you? -$seed$),
  (20, 11, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$فَلَمَّآ أَتَىٰهَا نُودِىَ يَٰمُوسَىٰٓ$seed$, $seed$And when he came to it, he was called, "O Moses,$seed$),
  (20, 13, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$وَأَنَا ٱخْتَرْتُكَ فَٱسْتَمِعْ لِمَا يُوحَىٰٓ$seed$, $seed$And I have chosen you, so listen to what is revealed [to you].$seed$),
  (20, 17, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$وَمَا تِلْكَ بِيَمِينِكَ يَٰمُوسَىٰ$seed$, $seed$And what is that in your right hand, O Moses?"$seed$),
  (20, 19, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$قَالَ أَلْقِهَا يَٰمُوسَىٰ$seed$, $seed$[Allah] said, "Throw it down, O Moses."$seed$),
  (20, 20, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$فَأَلْقَىٰهَا فَإِذَا هِىَ حَيَّةٌۭ تَسْعَىٰ$seed$, $seed$So he threw it down, and thereupon it was a snake, moving swiftly.$seed$),
  (20, 23, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$لِنُرِيَكَ مِنْ ءَايَٰتِنَا ٱلْكُبْرَى$seed$, $seed$That We may show you [some] of Our greater signs.$seed$),
  (20, 24, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$ٱذْهَبْ إِلَىٰ فِرْعَوْنَ إِنَّهُۥ طَغَىٰ$seed$, $seed$Go to Pharaoh. Indeed, he has transgressed."$seed$),
  (20, 25, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$قَالَ رَبِّ ٱشْرَحْ لِى صَدْرِى$seed$, $seed$[Moses] said, "My Lord, expand for me my breast [with assurance]$seed$),
  (20, 26, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$وَيَسِّرْ لِىٓ أَمْرِى$seed$, $seed$And ease for me my task$seed$),
  (20, 27, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$وَٱحْلُلْ عُقْدَةًۭ مِّن لِّسَانِى$seed$, $seed$And untie the knot from my tongue$seed$),
  (20, 28, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$يَفْقَهُوا۟ قَوْلِى$seed$, $seed$That they may understand my speech.$seed$),
  (20, 29, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$وَٱجْعَل لِّى وَزِيرًۭا مِّنْ أَهْلِى$seed$, $seed$And appoint for me a minister from my family -$seed$),
  (20, 30, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$هَٰرُونَ أَخِى$seed$, $seed$Aaron, my brother.$seed$),
  (20, 31, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$ٱشْدُدْ بِهِۦٓ أَزْرِى$seed$, $seed$Increase through him my strength$seed$),
  (20, 32, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$وَأَشْرِكْهُ فِىٓ أَمْرِى$seed$, $seed$And let him share my task$seed$),
  (20, 33, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$كَىْ نُسَبِّحَكَ كَثِيرًۭا$seed$, $seed$That we may exalt You much$seed$),
  (20, 34, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$وَنَذْكُرَكَ كَثِيرًا$seed$, $seed$And remember You much.$seed$),
  (20, 35, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$إِنَّكَ كُنتَ بِنَا بَصِيرًۭا$seed$, $seed$Indeed, You are of us ever Seeing."$seed$),
  (20, 36, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$قَالَ قَدْ أُوتِيتَ سُؤْلَكَ يَٰمُوسَىٰ$seed$, $seed$[Allah] said, "You have been granted your request, O Moses.$seed$),
  (20, 37, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$وَلَقَدْ مَنَنَّا عَلَيْكَ مَرَّةً أُخْرَىٰٓ$seed$, $seed$And We had already conferred favor upon you another time,$seed$),
  (20, 38, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$إِذْ أَوْحَيْنَآ إِلَىٰٓ أُمِّكَ مَا يُوحَىٰٓ$seed$, $seed$When We inspired to your mother what We inspired,$seed$),
  (20, 41, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$وَٱصْطَنَعْتُكَ لِنَفْسِى$seed$, $seed$And I produced you for Myself.$seed$),
  (20, 43, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$ٱذْهَبَآ إِلَىٰ فِرْعَوْنَ إِنَّهُۥ طَغَىٰ$seed$, $seed$Go, both of you, to Pharaoh. Indeed, he has transgressed.$seed$),
  (20, 49, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$قَالَ فَمَن رَّبُّكُمَا يَٰمُوسَىٰ$seed$, $seed$[Pharaoh] said, "So who is the Lord of you two, O Moses?"$seed$),
  (20, 51, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$قَالَ فَمَا بَالُ ٱلْقُرُونِ ٱلْأُولَىٰ$seed$, $seed$[Pharaoh] said, "Then what is the case of the former generations?"$seed$),
  (20, 60, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$فَتَوَلَّىٰ فِرْعَوْنُ فَجَمَعَ كَيْدَهُۥ ثُمَّ أَتَىٰ$seed$, $seed$So Pharaoh went away, put together his plan, and then came [to Moses].$seed$),
  (20, 67, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$فَأَوْجَسَ فِى نَفْسِهِۦ خِيفَةًۭ مُّوسَىٰ$seed$, $seed$And he sensed within himself apprehension, did Moses.$seed$),
  (20, 68, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$قُلْنَا لَا تَخَفْ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلْأَعْلَىٰ$seed$, $seed$Allah said, "Fear not. Indeed, it is you who are superior.$seed$),
  (20, 79, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$وَأَضَلَّ فِرْعَوْنُ قَوْمَهُۥ وَمَا هَدَىٰ$seed$, $seed$And Pharaoh led his people astray and did not guide [them].$seed$),
  (20, 83, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$۞ وَمَآ أَعْجَلَكَ عَن قَوْمِكَ يَٰمُوسَىٰ$seed$, $seed$[Allah] said, "And what made you hasten from your people, O Moses?"$seed$),
  (20, 93, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$أَلَّا تَتَّبِعَنِ ۖ أَفَعَصَيْتَ أَمْرِى$seed$, $seed$From following me? Then have you disobeyed my order?"$seed$),
  (20, 95, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$قَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكَ يَٰسَٰمِرِىُّ$seed$, $seed$[Moses] said, "And what is your case, O Samiri?"$seed$),
  (20, 106, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$فَيَذَرُهَا قَاعًۭا صَفْصَفًۭا$seed$, $seed$And He will leave the earth a level plain;$seed$),
  (20, 107, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$لَّا تَرَىٰ فِيهَا عِوَجًۭا وَلَآ أَمْتًۭا$seed$, $seed$You will not see therein a depression or an elevation."$seed$),
  (20, 118, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$إِنَّ لَكَ أَلَّا تَجُوعَ فِيهَا وَلَا تَعْرَىٰ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, it is [promised] for you not to be hungry therein or be unclothed.$seed$),
  (20, 119, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$وَأَنَّكَ لَا تَظْمَؤُا۟ فِيهَا وَلَا تَضْحَىٰ$seed$, $seed$And indeed, you will not be thirsty therein or be hot from the sun."$seed$),
  (20, 122, $seed$Taa-Haa$seed$, $seed$ثُمَّ ٱجْتَبَٰهُ رَبُّهُۥ فَتَابَ عَلَيْهِ وَهَدَىٰ$seed$, $seed$Then his Lord chose him and turned to him in forgiveness and guided [him].$seed$),
  (21, 14, $seed$Al-Anbiyaa$seed$, $seed$قَالُوا۟ يَٰوَيْلَنَآ إِنَّا كُنَّا ظَٰلِمِينَ$seed$, $seed$They said, "O woe to us! Indeed, we were wrongdoers."$seed$),
  (21, 20, $seed$Al-Anbiyaa$seed$, $seed$يُسَبِّحُونَ ٱلَّيْلَ وَٱلنَّهَارَ لَا يَفْتُرُونَ$seed$, $seed$They exalt [Him] night and day [and] do not slacken.$seed$),
  (21, 23, $seed$Al-Anbiyaa$seed$, $seed$لَا يُسْـَٔلُ عَمَّا يَفْعَلُ وَهُمْ يُسْـَٔلُونَ$seed$, $seed$He is not questioned about what He does, but they will be questioned.$seed$),
  (21, 53, $seed$Al-Anbiyaa$seed$, $seed$قَالُوا۟ وَجَدْنَآ ءَابَآءَنَا لَهَا عَٰبِدِينَ$seed$, $seed$They said, "We found our fathers worshippers of them."$seed$),
  (21, 106, $seed$Al-Anbiyaa$seed$, $seed$إِنَّ فِى هَٰذَا لَبَلَٰغًۭا لِّقَوْمٍ عَٰبِدِينَ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, in this [Qur'an] is notification for a worshipping people.$seed$),
  (21, 107, $seed$Al-Anbiyaa$seed$, $seed$وَمَآ أَرْسَلْنَٰكَ إِلَّا رَحْمَةًۭ لِّلْعَٰلَمِينَ$seed$, $seed$And We have not sent you, [O Muhammad], except as a mercy to the worlds.$seed$),
  (22, 20, $seed$Al-Hajj$seed$, $seed$يُصْهَرُ بِهِۦ مَا فِى بُطُونِهِمْ وَٱلْجُلُودُ$seed$, $seed$By which is melted that within their bellies and [their] skins.$seed$),
  (22, 21, $seed$Al-Hajj$seed$, $seed$وَلَهُم مَّقَٰمِعُ مِنْ حَدِيدٍۢ$seed$, $seed$And for [striking] them are maces of iron.$seed$),
  (22, 43, $seed$Al-Hajj$seed$, $seed$وَقَوْمُ إِبْرَٰهِيمَ وَقَوْمُ لُوطٍۢ$seed$, $seed$And the people of Abraham and the people of Lot$seed$),
  (23, 1, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$قَدْ أَفْلَحَ ٱلْمُؤْمِنُونَ$seed$, $seed$Certainly will the believers have succeeded:$seed$),
  (23, 2, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$ٱلَّذِينَ هُمْ فِى صَلَاتِهِمْ خَٰشِعُونَ$seed$, $seed$They who are during their prayer humbly submissive$seed$),
  (23, 3, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$وَٱلَّذِينَ هُمْ عَنِ ٱللَّغْوِ مُعْرِضُونَ$seed$, $seed$And they who turn away from ill speech$seed$),
  (23, 4, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$وَٱلَّذِينَ هُمْ لِلزَّكَوٰةِ فَٰعِلُونَ$seed$, $seed$And they who are observant of zakah$seed$),
  (23, 5, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$وَٱلَّذِينَ هُمْ لِفُرُوجِهِمْ حَٰفِظُونَ$seed$, $seed$And they who guard their private parts$seed$),
  (23, 8, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$وَٱلَّذِينَ هُمْ لِأَمَٰنَٰتِهِمْ وَعَهْدِهِمْ رَٰعُونَ$seed$, $seed$And they who are to their trusts and their promises attentive$seed$),
  (23, 9, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$وَٱلَّذِينَ هُمْ عَلَىٰ صَلَوَٰتِهِمْ يُحَافِظُونَ$seed$, $seed$And they who carefully maintain their prayers -$seed$),
  (23, 10, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلْوَٰرِثُونَ$seed$, $seed$Those are the inheritors$seed$),
  (23, 13, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$ثُمَّ جَعَلْنَٰهُ نُطْفَةًۭ فِى قَرَارٍۢ مَّكِينٍۢ$seed$, $seed$Then We placed him as a sperm-drop in a firm lodging.$seed$),
  (23, 15, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$ثُمَّ إِنَّكُم بَعْدَ ذَٰلِكَ لَمَيِّتُونَ$seed$, $seed$Then indeed, after that you are to die.$seed$),
  (23, 16, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$ثُمَّ إِنَّكُمْ يَوْمَ ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ تُبْعَثُونَ$seed$, $seed$Then indeed you, on the Day of Resurrection, will be resurrected.$seed$),
  (23, 22, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$وَعَلَيْهَا وَعَلَى ٱلْفُلْكِ تُحْمَلُونَ$seed$, $seed$And upon them and on ships you are carried.$seed$),
  (23, 26, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$قَالَ رَبِّ ٱنصُرْنِى بِمَا كَذَّبُونِ$seed$, $seed$[Noah] said, "My Lord, support me because they have denied me."$seed$),
  (23, 36, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$۞ هَيْهَاتَ هَيْهَاتَ لِمَا تُوعَدُونَ$seed$, $seed$How far, how far, is that which you are promised.$seed$),
  (23, 39, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$قَالَ رَبِّ ٱنصُرْنِى بِمَا كَذَّبُونِ$seed$, $seed$He said, "My Lord, support me because they have denied me."$seed$),
  (23, 40, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$قَالَ عَمَّا قَلِيلٍۢ لَّيُصْبِحُنَّ نَٰدِمِينَ$seed$, $seed$[Allah] said, "After a little, they will surely become regretful."$seed$),
  (23, 48, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$فَكَذَّبُوهُمَا فَكَانُوا۟ مِنَ ٱلْمُهْلَكِينَ$seed$, $seed$So they denied them and were of those destroyed.$seed$),
  (23, 54, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$فَذَرْهُمْ فِى غَمْرَتِهِمْ حَتَّىٰ حِينٍ$seed$, $seed$So leave them in their confusion for a time.$seed$),
  (23, 58, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$وَٱلَّذِينَ هُم بِـَٔايَٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ يُؤْمِنُونَ$seed$, $seed$And they who believe in the signs of their Lord$seed$),
  (23, 59, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$وَٱلَّذِينَ هُم بِرَبِّهِمْ لَا يُشْرِكُونَ$seed$, $seed$And they who do not associate anything with their Lord$seed$),
  (23, 67, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$مُسْتَكْبِرِينَ بِهِۦ سَٰمِرًۭا تَهْجُرُونَ$seed$, $seed$In arrogance regarding it, conversing by night, speaking evil.$seed$),
  (23, 73, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$وَإِنَّكَ لَتَدْعُوهُمْ إِلَىٰ صِرَٰطٍۢ مُّسْتَقِيمٍۢ$seed$, $seed$And indeed, you invite them to a straight path.$seed$),
  (23, 81, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$بَلْ قَالُوا۟ مِثْلَ مَا قَالَ ٱلْأَوَّلُونَ$seed$, $seed$Rather, they say like what the former peoples said.$seed$),
  (23, 85, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$سَيَقُولُونَ لِلَّهِ ۚ قُلْ أَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُونَ$seed$, $seed$They will say, "To Allah." Say, "Then will you not remember?"$seed$),
  (23, 87, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$سَيَقُولُونَ لِلَّهِ ۚ قُلْ أَفَلَا تَتَّقُونَ$seed$, $seed$They will say, "[They belong] to Allah." Say, "Then will you not fear Him?"$seed$),
  (23, 89, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$سَيَقُولُونَ لِلَّهِ ۚ قُلْ فَأَنَّىٰ تُسْحَرُونَ$seed$, $seed$They will say, "[All belongs] to Allah." Say, "Then how are you deluded?"$seed$),
  (23, 90, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$بَلْ أَتَيْنَٰهُم بِٱلْحَقِّ وَإِنَّهُمْ لَكَٰذِبُونَ$seed$, $seed$Rather, We have brought them the truth, and indeed they are liars.$seed$),
  (23, 93, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$قُل رَّبِّ إِمَّا تُرِيَنِّى مَا يُوعَدُونَ$seed$, $seed$Say, [O Muhammad], "My Lord, if You should show me that which they are promised,$seed$),
  (23, 98, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$وَأَعُوذُ بِكَ رَبِّ أَن يَحْضُرُونِ$seed$, $seed$And I seek refuge in You, my Lord, lest they be present with me."$seed$),
  (23, 108, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$قَالَ ٱخْسَـُٔوا۟ فِيهَا وَلَا تُكَلِّمُونِ$seed$, $seed$He will say, "Remain despised therein and do not speak to Me.$seed$),
  (23, 112, $seed$Al-Muminoon$seed$, $seed$قَٰلَ كَمْ لَبِثْتُمْ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ عَدَدَ سِنِينَ$seed$, $seed$[Allah] will say, "How long did you remain on earth in number of years?"$seed$),
  (25, 46, $seed$Al-Furqaan$seed$, $seed$ثُمَّ قَبَضْنَٰهُ إِلَيْنَا قَبْضًۭا يَسِيرًۭا$seed$, $seed$Then We hold it in hand for a brief grasp.$seed$),
  (25, 56, $seed$Al-Furqaan$seed$, $seed$وَمَآ أَرْسَلْنَٰكَ إِلَّا مُبَشِّرًۭا وَنَذِيرًۭا$seed$, $seed$And We have not sent you, [O Muhammad], except as a bringer of good tidings and a warner.$seed$),
  (25, 66, $seed$Al-Furqaan$seed$, $seed$إِنَّهَا سَآءَتْ مُسْتَقَرًّۭا وَمُقَامًۭا$seed$, $seed$Indeed, it is evil as a settlement and residence."$seed$),
  (26, 1, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$طسٓمٓ$seed$, $seed$Ta, Seen, Meem.$seed$),
  (26, 2, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$تِلْكَ ءَايَٰتُ ٱلْكِتَٰبِ ٱلْمُبِينِ$seed$, $seed$These are the verses of the clear Book.$seed$),
  (26, 9, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ ٱلْعَزِيزُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ$seed$, $seed$And indeed, your Lord - He is the Exalted in Might, the Merciful.$seed$),
  (26, 11, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$قَوْمَ فِرْعَوْنَ ۚ أَلَا يَتَّقُونَ$seed$, $seed$The people of Pharaoh. Will they not fear Allah?"$seed$),
  (26, 12, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$قَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّىٓ أَخَافُ أَن يُكَذِّبُونِ$seed$, $seed$He said, "My Lord, indeed I fear that they will deny me$seed$),
  (26, 14, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَلَهُمْ عَلَىَّ ذَنۢبٌۭ فَأَخَافُ أَن يَقْتُلُونِ$seed$, $seed$And they have upon me a [claim due to] sin, so I fear that they will kill me."$seed$),
  (26, 17, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$أَنْ أَرْسِلْ مَعَنَا بَنِىٓ إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ$seed$, $seed$[Commanded to say], "Send with us the Children of Israel."'"$seed$),
  (26, 23, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$قَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ وَمَا رَبُّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ$seed$, $seed$Said Pharaoh, "And what is the Lord of the worlds?"$seed$),
  (26, 25, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$قَالَ لِمَنْ حَوْلَهُۥٓ أَلَا تَسْتَمِعُونَ$seed$, $seed$[Pharaoh] said to those around him, "Do you not hear?"$seed$),
  (26, 26, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$قَالَ رَبُّكُمْ وَرَبُّ ءَابَآئِكُمُ ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ$seed$, $seed$[Moses] said, "Your Lord and the Lord of your first forefathers."$seed$),
  (26, 30, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$قَالَ أَوَلَوْ جِئْتُكَ بِشَىْءٍۢ مُّبِينٍۢ$seed$, $seed$[Moses] said, "Even if I brought you proof manifest?"$seed$),
  (26, 31, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$قَالَ فَأْتِ بِهِۦٓ إِن كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ$seed$, $seed$[Pharaoh] said, "Then bring it, if you should be of the truthful."$seed$),
  (26, 32, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$فَأَلْقَىٰ عَصَاهُ فَإِذَا هِىَ ثُعْبَانٌۭ مُّبِينٌۭ$seed$, $seed$So [Moses] threw his staff, and suddenly it was a serpent manifest.$seed$),
  (26, 37, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$يَأْتُوكَ بِكُلِّ سَحَّارٍ عَلِيمٍۢ$seed$, $seed$Who will bring you every learned, skilled magician."$seed$),
  (26, 38, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$فَجُمِعَ ٱلسَّحَرَةُ لِمِيقَٰتِ يَوْمٍۢ مَّعْلُومٍۢ$seed$, $seed$So the magicians were assembled for the appointment of a well-known day.$seed$),
  (26, 39, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَقِيلَ لِلنَّاسِ هَلْ أَنتُم مُّجْتَمِعُونَ$seed$, $seed$And it was said to the people, "Will you congregate$seed$),
  (26, 46, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$فَأُلْقِىَ ٱلسَّحَرَةُ سَٰجِدِينَ$seed$, $seed$So the magicians fell down in prostration [to Allah].$seed$),
  (26, 47, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$قَالُوٓا۟ ءَامَنَّا بِرَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ$seed$, $seed$They said, "We have believed in the Lord of the worlds,$seed$),
  (26, 48, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$رَبِّ مُوسَىٰ وَهَٰرُونَ$seed$, $seed$The Lord of Moses and Aaron."$seed$),
  (26, 53, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$فَأَرْسَلَ فِرْعَوْنُ فِى ٱلْمَدَآئِنِ حَٰشِرِينَ$seed$, $seed$Then Pharaoh sent among the cities gatherers$seed$),
  (26, 54, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$إِنَّ هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ لَشِرْذِمَةٌۭ قَلِيلُونَ$seed$, $seed$[And said], "Indeed, those are but a small band,$seed$),
  (26, 55, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَإِنَّهُمْ لَنَا لَغَآئِظُونَ$seed$, $seed$And indeed, they are enraging us,$seed$),
  (26, 56, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَإِنَّا لَجَمِيعٌ حَٰذِرُونَ$seed$, $seed$And indeed, we are a cautious society... "$seed$),
  (26, 57, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$فَأَخْرَجْنَٰهُم مِّن جَنَّٰتٍۢ وَعُيُونٍۢ$seed$, $seed$So We removed them from gardens and springs$seed$),
  (26, 58, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَكُنُوزٍۢ وَمَقَامٍۢ كَرِيمٍۢ$seed$, $seed$And treasures and honorable station -$seed$),
  (26, 59, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$كَذَٰلِكَ وَأَوْرَثْنَٰهَا بَنِىٓ إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ$seed$, $seed$Thus. And We caused to inherit it the Children of Israel.$seed$),
  (26, 60, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$فَأَتْبَعُوهُم مُّشْرِقِينَ$seed$, $seed$So they pursued them at sunrise.$seed$),
  (26, 62, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$قَالَ كَلَّآ ۖ إِنَّ مَعِىَ رَبِّى سَيَهْدِينِ$seed$, $seed$[Moses] said, "No! Indeed, with me is my Lord; He will guide me."$seed$),
  (26, 64, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَأَزْلَفْنَا ثَمَّ ٱلْءَاخَرِينَ$seed$, $seed$And We advanced thereto the pursuers.$seed$),
  (26, 65, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَأَنجَيْنَا مُوسَىٰ وَمَن مَّعَهُۥٓ أَجْمَعِينَ$seed$, $seed$And We saved Moses and those with him, all together.$seed$),
  (26, 66, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$ثُمَّ أَغْرَقْنَا ٱلْءَاخَرِينَ$seed$, $seed$Then We drowned the others.$seed$),
  (26, 68, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ ٱلْعَزِيزُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ$seed$, $seed$And indeed, your Lord - He is the Exalted in Might, the Merciful.$seed$),
  (26, 69, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَٱتْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ نَبَأَ إِبْرَٰهِيمَ$seed$, $seed$And recite to them the news of Abraham,$seed$),
  (26, 70, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$إِذْ قَالَ لِأَبِيهِ وَقَوْمِهِۦ مَا تَعْبُدُونَ$seed$, $seed$When he said to his father and his people, "What do you worship?"$seed$),
  (26, 72, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$قَالَ هَلْ يَسْمَعُونَكُمْ إِذْ تَدْعُونَ$seed$, $seed$He said, "Do they hear you when you supplicate?$seed$),
  (26, 73, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$أَوْ يَنفَعُونَكُمْ أَوْ يَضُرُّونَ$seed$, $seed$Or do they benefit you, or do they harm?"$seed$),
  (26, 75, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$قَالَ أَفَرَءَيْتُم مَّا كُنتُمْ تَعْبُدُونَ$seed$, $seed$He said, "Then do you see what you have been worshipping,$seed$),
  (26, 76, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$أَنتُمْ وَءَابَآؤُكُمُ ٱلْأَقْدَمُونَ$seed$, $seed$You and your ancient forefathers?$seed$),
  (26, 77, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$فَإِنَّهُمْ عَدُوٌّۭ لِّىٓ إِلَّا رَبَّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, they are enemies to me, except the Lord of the worlds,$seed$),
  (26, 78, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$ٱلَّذِى خَلَقَنِى فَهُوَ يَهْدِينِ$seed$, $seed$Who created me, and He [it is who] guides me.$seed$),
  (26, 79, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَٱلَّذِى هُوَ يُطْعِمُنِى وَيَسْقِينِ$seed$, $seed$And it is He who feeds me and gives me drink.$seed$),
  (26, 80, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَإِذَا مَرِضْتُ فَهُوَ يَشْفِينِ$seed$, $seed$And when I am ill, it is He who cures me$seed$),
  (26, 81, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَٱلَّذِى يُمِيتُنِى ثُمَّ يُحْيِينِ$seed$, $seed$And who will cause me to die and then bring me to life$seed$),
  (26, 84, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَٱجْعَل لِّى لِسَانَ صِدْقٍۢ فِى ٱلْءَاخِرِينَ$seed$, $seed$And grant me a reputation of honor among later generations.$seed$),
  (26, 85, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَٱجْعَلْنِى مِن وَرَثَةِ جَنَّةِ ٱلنَّعِيمِ$seed$, $seed$And place me among the inheritors of the Garden of Pleasure.$seed$),
  (26, 87, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَلَا تُخْزِنِى يَوْمَ يُبْعَثُونَ$seed$, $seed$And do not disgrace me on the Day they are [all] resurrected -$seed$),
  (26, 88, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$يَوْمَ لَا يَنفَعُ مَالٌۭ وَلَا بَنُونَ$seed$, $seed$The Day when there will not benefit [anyone] wealth or children$seed$),
  (26, 89, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$إِلَّا مَنْ أَتَى ٱللَّهَ بِقَلْبٍۢ سَلِيمٍۢ$seed$, $seed$But only one who comes to Allah with a sound heart."$seed$),
  (26, 90, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَأُزْلِفَتِ ٱلْجَنَّةُ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ$seed$, $seed$And Paradise will be brought near [that Day] to the righteous.$seed$),
  (26, 91, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَبُرِّزَتِ ٱلْجَحِيمُ لِلْغَاوِينَ$seed$, $seed$And Hellfire will be brought forth for the deviators,$seed$),
  (26, 92, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَقِيلَ لَهُمْ أَيْنَ مَا كُنتُمْ تَعْبُدُونَ$seed$, $seed$And it will be said to them, "Where are those you used to worship$seed$),
  (26, 94, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$فَكُبْكِبُوا۟ فِيهَا هُمْ وَٱلْغَاوُۥنَ$seed$, $seed$So they will be overturned into Hellfire, they and the deviators$seed$),
  (26, 95, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَجُنُودُ إِبْلِيسَ أَجْمَعُونَ$seed$, $seed$And the soldiers of Iblees, all together.$seed$),
  (26, 96, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$قَالُوا۟ وَهُمْ فِيهَا يَخْتَصِمُونَ$seed$, $seed$They will say while they dispute therein,$seed$),
  (26, 97, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$تَٱللَّهِ إِن كُنَّا لَفِى ضَلَٰلٍۢ مُّبِينٍ$seed$, $seed$"By Allah, we were indeed in manifest error$seed$),
  (26, 98, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$إِذْ نُسَوِّيكُم بِرَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ$seed$, $seed$When we equated you with the Lord of the worlds.$seed$),
  (26, 99, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَمَآ أَضَلَّنَآ إِلَّا ٱلْمُجْرِمُونَ$seed$, $seed$And no one misguided us except the criminals.$seed$),
  (26, 100, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$فَمَا لَنَا مِن شَٰفِعِينَ$seed$, $seed$So now we have no intercessors$seed$),
  (26, 101, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَلَا صَدِيقٍ حَمِيمٍۢ$seed$, $seed$And not a devoted friend.$seed$),
  (26, 104, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ ٱلْعَزِيزُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ$seed$, $seed$And indeed, your Lord - He is the Exalted in Might, the Merciful.$seed$),
  (26, 105, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$كَذَّبَتْ قَوْمُ نُوحٍ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ$seed$, $seed$The people of Noah denied the messengers$seed$),
  (26, 107, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$إِنِّى لَكُمْ رَسُولٌ أَمِينٌۭ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, I am to you a trustworthy messenger.$seed$),
  (26, 108, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$فَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُونِ$seed$, $seed$So fear Allah and obey me.$seed$),
  (26, 110, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$فَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُونِ$seed$, $seed$So fear Allah and obey me."$seed$),
  (26, 112, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$قَالَ وَمَا عِلْمِى بِمَا كَانُوا۟ يَعْمَلُونَ$seed$, $seed$He said, "And what is my knowledge of what they used to do?$seed$),
  (26, 114, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَمَآ أَنَا۠ بِطَارِدِ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ$seed$, $seed$And I am not one to drive away the believers.$seed$),
  (26, 115, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$إِنْ أَنَا۠ إِلَّا نَذِيرٌۭ مُّبِينٌۭ$seed$, $seed$I am only a clear warner."$seed$),
  (26, 117, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$قَالَ رَبِّ إِنَّ قَوْمِى كَذَّبُونِ$seed$, $seed$He said, "My Lord, indeed my people have denied me.$seed$),
  (26, 120, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$ثُمَّ أَغْرَقْنَا بَعْدُ ٱلْبَاقِينَ$seed$, $seed$Then We drowned thereafter the remaining ones.$seed$),
  (26, 122, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ ٱلْعَزِيزُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ$seed$, $seed$And indeed, your Lord - He is the Exalted in Might, the Merciful.$seed$),
  (26, 123, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$كَذَّبَتْ عَادٌ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ$seed$, $seed$'Aad denied the messengers$seed$),
  (26, 125, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$إِنِّى لَكُمْ رَسُولٌ أَمِينٌۭ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, I am to you a trustworthy messenger.$seed$),
  (26, 126, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$فَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُونِ$seed$, $seed$So fear Allah and obey me.$seed$),
  (26, 128, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$أَتَبْنُونَ بِكُلِّ رِيعٍ ءَايَةًۭ تَعْبَثُونَ$seed$, $seed$Do you construct on every elevation a sign, amusing yourselves,$seed$),
  (26, 129, $seed$Ash-Shu'araa$seed$, $seed$وَتَتَّخِذُونَ مَصَانِعَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَخْلُدُونَ$seed$, $seed$And take for yourselves palaces and fortresses that you might abide eternally?$seed$),
