  (36, 25, $seed$Yaseen$seed$, $seed$إِنِّىٓ ءَامَنتُ بِرَبِّكُمْ فَٱسْمَعُونِ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, I have believed in your Lord, so listen to me."$seed$),
  (36, 32, $seed$Yaseen$seed$, $seed$وَإِن كُلٌّۭ لَّمَّا جَمِيعٌۭ لَّدَيْنَا مُحْضَرُونَ$seed$, $seed$And indeed, all of them will yet be brought present before Us.$seed$),
  (36, 42, $seed$Yaseen$seed$, $seed$وَخَلَقْنَا لَهُم مِّن مِّثْلِهِۦ مَا يَرْكَبُونَ$seed$, $seed$And We created for them from the likes of it that which they ride.$seed$),
  (36, 44, $seed$Yaseen$seed$, $seed$إِلَّا رَحْمَةًۭ مِّنَّا وَمَتَٰعًا إِلَىٰ حِينٍۢ$seed$, $seed$Except as a mercy from Us and provision for a time.$seed$),
  (36, 57, $seed$Yaseen$seed$, $seed$لَهُمْ فِيهَا فَٰكِهَةٌۭ وَلَهُم مَّا يَدَّعُونَ$seed$, $seed$For them therein is fruit, and for them is whatever they request [or wish]$seed$),
  (36, 58, $seed$Yaseen$seed$, $seed$سَلَٰمٌۭ قَوْلًۭا مِّن رَّبٍّۢ رَّحِيمٍۢ$seed$, $seed$[And] "Peace," a word from a Merciful Lord.$seed$),
  (36, 59, $seed$Yaseen$seed$, $seed$وَٱمْتَٰزُوا۟ ٱلْيَوْمَ أَيُّهَا ٱلْمُجْرِمُونَ$seed$, $seed$[Then He will say], "But stand apart today, you criminals.$seed$),
  (36, 61, $seed$Yaseen$seed$, $seed$وَأَنِ ٱعْبُدُونِى ۚ هَٰذَا صِرَٰطٌۭ مُّسْتَقِيمٌۭ$seed$, $seed$And that you worship [only] Me? This is a straight path.$seed$),
  (36, 63, $seed$Yaseen$seed$, $seed$هَٰذِهِۦ جَهَنَّمُ ٱلَّتِى كُنتُمْ تُوعَدُونَ$seed$, $seed$This is the Hellfire which you were promised.$seed$),
  (36, 64, $seed$Yaseen$seed$, $seed$ٱصْلَوْهَا ٱلْيَوْمَ بِمَا كُنتُمْ تَكْفُرُونَ$seed$, $seed$[Enter to] burn therein today for what you used to deny."$seed$),
  (37, 1, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$وَٱلصَّٰٓفَّٰتِ صَفًّۭا$seed$, $seed$By those [angels] lined up in rows$seed$),
  (37, 2, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$فَٱلزَّٰجِرَٰتِ زَجْرًۭا$seed$, $seed$And those who drive [the clouds]$seed$),
  (37, 3, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$فَٱلتَّٰلِيَٰتِ ذِكْرًا$seed$, $seed$And those who recite the message,$seed$),
  (37, 4, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$إِنَّ إِلَٰهَكُمْ لَوَٰحِدٌۭ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, your God is One,$seed$),
  (37, 7, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$وَحِفْظًۭا مِّن كُلِّ شَيْطَٰنٍۢ مَّارِدٍۢ$seed$, $seed$And as protection against every rebellious devil$seed$),
  (37, 9, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$دُحُورًۭا ۖ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌۭ وَاصِبٌ$seed$, $seed$Repelled; and for them is a constant punishment,$seed$),
  (37, 12, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$بَلْ عَجِبْتَ وَيَسْخَرُونَ$seed$, $seed$But you wonder, while they mock,$seed$),
  (37, 13, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$وَإِذَا ذُكِّرُوا۟ لَا يَذْكُرُونَ$seed$, $seed$And when they are reminded, they remember not.$seed$),
  (37, 14, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$وَإِذَا رَأَوْا۟ ءَايَةًۭ يَسْتَسْخِرُونَ$seed$, $seed$And when they see a sign, they ridicule$seed$),
  (37, 15, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$وَقَالُوٓا۟ إِنْ هَٰذَآ إِلَّا سِحْرٌۭ مُّبِينٌ$seed$, $seed$And say, "This is not but obvious magic.$seed$),
  (37, 17, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$أَوَءَابَآؤُنَا ٱلْأَوَّلُونَ$seed$, $seed$And our forefathers [as well]?"$seed$),
  (37, 18, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$قُلْ نَعَمْ وَأَنتُمْ دَٰخِرُونَ$seed$, $seed$Say, "Yes, and you will be [rendered] contemptible."$seed$),
  (37, 20, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$وَقَالُوا۟ يَٰوَيْلَنَا هَٰذَا يَوْمُ ٱلدِّينِ$seed$, $seed$They will say, "O woe to us! This is the Day of Recompense."$seed$),
  (37, 24, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$وَقِفُوهُمْ ۖ إِنَّهُم مَّسْـُٔولُونَ$seed$, $seed$And stop them; indeed, they are to be questioned."$seed$),
  (37, 25, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$مَا لَكُمْ لَا تَنَاصَرُونَ$seed$, $seed$[They will be asked], "What is [wrong] with you? Why do you not help each other?"$seed$),
  (37, 26, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$بَلْ هُمُ ٱلْيَوْمَ مُسْتَسْلِمُونَ$seed$, $seed$But they, that Day, are in surrender.$seed$),
  (37, 27, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$وَأَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍۢ يَتَسَآءَلُونَ$seed$, $seed$And they will approach one another blaming each other.$seed$),
  (37, 29, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$قَالُوا۟ بَل لَّمْ تَكُونُوا۟ مُؤْمِنِينَ$seed$, $seed$The oppressors will say, "Rather, you [yourselves] were not believers,$seed$),
  (37, 32, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$فَأَغْوَيْنَٰكُمْ إِنَّا كُنَّا غَٰوِينَ$seed$, $seed$And we led you to deviation; indeed, we were deviators."$seed$),
  (37, 33, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$فَإِنَّهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍۢ فِى ٱلْعَذَابِ مُشْتَرِكُونَ$seed$, $seed$So indeed they, that Day, will be sharing in the punishment.$seed$),
  (37, 34, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$إِنَّا كَذَٰلِكَ نَفْعَلُ بِٱلْمُجْرِمِينَ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, that is how We deal with the criminals.$seed$),
  (37, 37, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$بَلْ جَآءَ بِٱلْحَقِّ وَصَدَّقَ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ$seed$, $seed$Rather, the Prophet has come with the truth and confirmed the [previous] messengers.$seed$),
  (37, 38, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$إِنَّكُمْ لَذَآئِقُوا۟ ٱلْعَذَابِ ٱلْأَلِيمِ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, you [disbelievers] will be tasters of the painful punishment,$seed$),
  (37, 39, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$وَمَا تُجْزَوْنَ إِلَّا مَا كُنتُمْ تَعْمَلُونَ$seed$, $seed$And you will not be recompensed except for what you used to do -$seed$),
  (37, 40, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$إِلَّا عِبَادَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلْمُخْلَصِينَ$seed$, $seed$But not the chosen servants of Allah.$seed$),
  (37, 41, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ رِزْقٌۭ مَّعْلُومٌۭ$seed$, $seed$Those will have a provision determined -$seed$),
  (37, 42, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$فَوَٰكِهُ ۖ وَهُم مُّكْرَمُونَ$seed$, $seed$Fruits; and they will be honored$seed$),
  (37, 43, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$فِى جَنَّٰتِ ٱلنَّعِيمِ$seed$, $seed$In gardens of pleasure$seed$),
  (37, 44, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$عَلَىٰ سُرُرٍۢ مُّتَقَٰبِلِينَ$seed$, $seed$On thrones facing one another.$seed$),
  (37, 45, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$يُطَافُ عَلَيْهِم بِكَأْسٍۢ مِّن مَّعِينٍۭ$seed$, $seed$There will be circulated among them a cup [of wine] from a flowing spring,$seed$),
  (37, 46, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$بَيْضَآءَ لَذَّةٍۢ لِّلشَّٰرِبِينَ$seed$, $seed$White and delicious to the drinkers;$seed$),
  (37, 48, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$وَعِندَهُمْ قَٰصِرَٰتُ ٱلطَّرْفِ عِينٌۭ$seed$, $seed$And with them will be women limiting [their] glances, with large, [beautiful] eyes,$seed$),
  (37, 49, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$كَأَنَّهُنَّ بَيْضٌۭ مَّكْنُونٌۭ$seed$, $seed$As if they were [delicate] eggs, well-protected.$seed$),
  (37, 50, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$فَأَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍۢ يَتَسَآءَلُونَ$seed$, $seed$And they will approach one another, inquiring of each other.$seed$),
  (37, 51, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$قَالَ قَآئِلٌۭ مِّنْهُمْ إِنِّى كَانَ لِى قَرِينٌۭ$seed$, $seed$A speaker among them will say, "Indeed, I had a companion [on earth]$seed$),
  (37, 52, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$يَقُولُ أَءِنَّكَ لَمِنَ ٱلْمُصَدِّقِينَ$seed$, $seed$Who would say, 'Are you indeed of those who believe$seed$),
  (37, 54, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$قَالَ هَلْ أَنتُم مُّطَّلِعُونَ$seed$, $seed$He will say, "Would you [care to] look?"$seed$),
  (37, 55, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$فَٱطَّلَعَ فَرَءَاهُ فِى سَوَآءِ ٱلْجَحِيمِ$seed$, $seed$And he will look and see him in the midst of the Hellfire.$seed$),
  (37, 56, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$قَالَ تَٱللَّهِ إِن كِدتَّ لَتُرْدِينِ$seed$, $seed$He will say, "By Allah, you almost ruined me.$seed$),
  (37, 58, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$أَفَمَا نَحْنُ بِمَيِّتِينَ$seed$, $seed$Then, are we not to die$seed$),
  (37, 60, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَهُوَ ٱلْفَوْزُ ٱلْعَظِيمُ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, this is the great attainment.$seed$),
  (37, 61, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$لِمِثْلِ هَٰذَا فَلْيَعْمَلِ ٱلْعَٰمِلُونَ$seed$, $seed$For the like of this let the workers [on earth] work.$seed$),
  (37, 62, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$أَذَٰلِكَ خَيْرٌۭ نُّزُلًا أَمْ شَجَرَةُ ٱلزَّقُّومِ$seed$, $seed$Is Paradise a better accommodation or the tree of zaqqum?$seed$),
  (37, 63, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$إِنَّا جَعَلْنَٰهَا فِتْنَةًۭ لِّلظَّٰلِمِينَ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, We have made it a torment for the wrongdoers.$seed$),
  (37, 64, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$إِنَّهَا شَجَرَةٌۭ تَخْرُجُ فِىٓ أَصْلِ ٱلْجَحِيمِ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, it is a tree issuing from the bottom of the Hellfire,$seed$),
  (37, 65, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$طَلْعُهَا كَأَنَّهُۥ رُءُوسُ ٱلشَّيَٰطِينِ$seed$, $seed$Its emerging fruit as if it was heads of the devils.$seed$),
  (37, 67, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$ثُمَّ إِنَّ لَهُمْ عَلَيْهَا لَشَوْبًۭا مِّنْ حَمِيمٍۢ$seed$, $seed$Then indeed, they will have after it a mixture of scalding water.$seed$),
  (37, 68, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$ثُمَّ إِنَّ مَرْجِعَهُمْ لَإِلَى ٱلْجَحِيمِ$seed$, $seed$Then indeed, their return will be to the Hellfire.$seed$),
  (37, 69, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$إِنَّهُمْ أَلْفَوْا۟ ءَابَآءَهُمْ ضَآلِّينَ$seed$, $seed$Indeed they found their fathers astray.$seed$),
  (37, 70, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$فَهُمْ عَلَىٰٓ ءَاثَٰرِهِمْ يُهْرَعُونَ$seed$, $seed$So they hastened [to follow] in their footsteps.$seed$),
  (37, 71, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$وَلَقَدْ ضَلَّ قَبْلَهُمْ أَكْثَرُ ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ$seed$, $seed$And there had already strayed before them most of the former peoples,$seed$),
  (37, 72, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$وَلَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا فِيهِم مُّنذِرِينَ$seed$, $seed$And We had already sent among them warners.$seed$),
  (37, 73, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$فَٱنظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلْمُنذَرِينَ$seed$, $seed$Then look how was the end of those who were warned -$seed$),
  (37, 74, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$إِلَّا عِبَادَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلْمُخْلَصِينَ$seed$, $seed$But not the chosen servants of Allah.$seed$),
  (37, 76, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$وَنَجَّيْنَٰهُ وَأَهْلَهُۥ مِنَ ٱلْكَرْبِ ٱلْعَظِيمِ$seed$, $seed$And We saved him and his family from the great affliction.$seed$),
  (37, 77, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$وَجَعَلْنَا ذُرِّيَّتَهُۥ هُمُ ٱلْبَاقِينَ$seed$, $seed$And We made his descendants those remaining [on the earth]$seed$),
  (37, 78, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$وَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِى ٱلْءَاخِرِينَ$seed$, $seed$And left for him [favorable mention] among later generations:$seed$),
  (37, 79, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$سَلَٰمٌ عَلَىٰ نُوحٍۢ فِى ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ$seed$, $seed$"Peace upon Noah among the worlds."$seed$),
  (37, 80, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$إِنَّا كَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِى ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, We thus reward the doers of good.$seed$),
  (37, 81, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$إِنَّهُۥ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, he was of Our believing servants.$seed$),
  (37, 82, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$ثُمَّ أَغْرَقْنَا ٱلْءَاخَرِينَ$seed$, $seed$Then We drowned the disbelievers.$seed$),
  (37, 83, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$۞ وَإِنَّ مِن شِيعَتِهِۦ لَإِبْرَٰهِيمَ$seed$, $seed$And indeed, among his kind was Abraham,$seed$),
  (37, 84, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$إِذْ جَآءَ رَبَّهُۥ بِقَلْبٍۢ سَلِيمٍ$seed$, $seed$When he came to his Lord with a sound heart$seed$),
  (37, 86, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$أَئِفْكًا ءَالِهَةًۭ دُونَ ٱللَّهِ تُرِيدُونَ$seed$, $seed$Is it falsehood [as] gods other than Allah you desire?$seed$),
  (37, 87, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$فَمَا ظَنُّكُم بِرَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ$seed$, $seed$Then what is your thought about the Lord of the worlds?"$seed$),
  (37, 88, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$فَنَظَرَ نَظْرَةًۭ فِى ٱلنُّجُومِ$seed$, $seed$And he cast a look at the stars$seed$),
  (37, 89, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$فَقَالَ إِنِّى سَقِيمٌۭ$seed$, $seed$And said, "Indeed, I am [about to be] ill."$seed$),
  (37, 90, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$فَتَوَلَّوْا۟ عَنْهُ مُدْبِرِينَ$seed$, $seed$So they turned away from him, departing.$seed$),
  (37, 92, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$مَا لَكُمْ لَا تَنطِقُونَ$seed$, $seed$What is [wrong] with you that you do not speak?"$seed$),
  (37, 93, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$فَرَاغَ عَلَيْهِمْ ضَرْبًۢا بِٱلْيَمِينِ$seed$, $seed$And he turned upon them a blow with [his] right hand.$seed$),
  (37, 94, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$فَأَقْبَلُوٓا۟ إِلَيْهِ يَزِفُّونَ$seed$, $seed$Then the people came toward him, hastening.$seed$),
  (37, 95, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$قَالَ أَتَعْبُدُونَ مَا تَنْحِتُونَ$seed$, $seed$He said, "Do you worship that which you [yourselves] carve,$seed$),
  (37, 96, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$وَٱللَّهُ خَلَقَكُمْ وَمَا تَعْمَلُونَ$seed$, $seed$While Allah created you and that which you do?"$seed$),
  (37, 99, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$وَقَالَ إِنِّى ذَاهِبٌ إِلَىٰ رَبِّى سَيَهْدِينِ$seed$, $seed$And [then] he said, "Indeed, I will go to [where I am ordered by] my Lord; He will guide me.$seed$),
  (37, 100, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$رَبِّ هَبْ لِى مِنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ$seed$, $seed$My Lord, grant me [a child] from among the righteous."$seed$),
  (37, 101, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$فَبَشَّرْنَٰهُ بِغُلَٰمٍ حَلِيمٍۢ$seed$, $seed$So We gave him good tidings of a forbearing boy.$seed$),
  (37, 103, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$فَلَمَّآ أَسْلَمَا وَتَلَّهُۥ لِلْجَبِينِ$seed$, $seed$And when they had both submitted and he put him down upon his forehead,$seed$),
  (37, 104, $seed$As-Saaffaat$seed$, $seed$وَنَٰدَيْنَٰهُ أَن يَٰٓإِبْرَٰهِيمُ$seed$, $seed$We called to him, "O Abraham,$seed$),
