  (38, 19, $seed$Saad$seed$, $seed$وَٱلطَّيْرَ مَحْشُورَةًۭ ۖ كُلٌّۭ لَّهُۥٓ أَوَّابٌۭ$seed$, $seed$And the birds were assembled, all with him repeating [praises].$seed$),
  (38, 37, $seed$Saad$seed$, $seed$وَٱلشَّيَٰطِينَ كُلَّ بَنَّآءٍۢ وَغَوَّاصٍۢ$seed$, $seed$And [also] the devils [of jinn] - every builder and diver$seed$),
  (38, 38, $seed$Saad$seed$, $seed$وَءَاخَرِينَ مُقَرَّنِينَ فِى ٱلْأَصْفَادِ$seed$, $seed$And others bound together in shackles.$seed$),
  (38, 40, $seed$Saad$seed$, $seed$وَإِنَّ لَهُۥ عِندَنَا لَزُلْفَىٰ وَحُسْنَ مَـَٔابٍۢ$seed$, $seed$And indeed, for him is nearness to Us and a good place of return.$seed$),
  (38, 46, $seed$Saad$seed$, $seed$إِنَّآ أَخْلَصْنَٰهُم بِخَالِصَةٍۢ ذِكْرَى ٱلدَّارِ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, We chose them for an exclusive quality: remembrance of the home [of the Hereafter].$seed$),
  (38, 50, $seed$Saad$seed$, $seed$جَنَّٰتِ عَدْنٍۢ مُّفَتَّحَةًۭ لَّهُمُ ٱلْأَبْوَٰبُ$seed$, $seed$Gardens of perpetual residence, whose doors will be opened to them.$seed$),
  (38, 52, $seed$Saad$seed$, $seed$۞ وَعِندَهُمْ قَٰصِرَٰتُ ٱلطَّرْفِ أَتْرَابٌ$seed$, $seed$And with them will be women limiting [their] glances and of equal age.$seed$),
  (38, 53, $seed$Saad$seed$, $seed$هَٰذَا مَا تُوعَدُونَ لِيَوْمِ ٱلْحِسَابِ$seed$, $seed$This is what you, [the righteous], are promised for the Day of Account.$seed$),
  (38, 54, $seed$Saad$seed$, $seed$إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَرِزْقُنَا مَا لَهُۥ مِن نَّفَادٍ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, this is Our provision; for it there is no depletion.$seed$),
  (38, 55, $seed$Saad$seed$, $seed$هَٰذَا ۚ وَإِنَّ لِلطَّٰغِينَ لَشَرَّ مَـَٔابٍۢ$seed$, $seed$This [is so]. But indeed, for the transgressors is an evil place of return -$seed$),
  (38, 56, $seed$Saad$seed$, $seed$جَهَنَّمَ يَصْلَوْنَهَا فَبِئْسَ ٱلْمِهَادُ$seed$, $seed$Hell, which they will [enter to] burn, and wretched is the resting place.$seed$),
  (38, 57, $seed$Saad$seed$, $seed$هَٰذَا فَلْيَذُوقُوهُ حَمِيمٌۭ وَغَسَّاقٌۭ$seed$, $seed$This - so let them taste it - is scalding water and [foul] purulence.$seed$),
  (38, 58, $seed$Saad$seed$, $seed$وَءَاخَرُ مِن شَكْلِهِۦٓ أَزْوَٰجٌ$seed$, $seed$And other [punishments] of its type [in various] kinds.$seed$),
  (38, 64, $seed$Saad$seed$, $seed$إِنَّ ذَٰلِكَ لَحَقٌّۭ تَخَاصُمُ أَهْلِ ٱلنَّارِ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, that is truth - the quarreling of the people of the Fire.$seed$),
