  (51, 11, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$ٱلَّذِينَ هُمْ فِى غَمْرَةٍۢ سَاهُونَ$seed$, $seed$Who are within a flood [of confusion] and heedless.$seed$),
  (51, 12, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$يَسْـَٔلُونَ أَيَّانَ يَوْمُ ٱلدِّينِ$seed$, $seed$They ask, "When is the Day of Recompense?"$seed$),
  (51, 13, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$يَوْمَ هُمْ عَلَى ٱلنَّارِ يُفْتَنُونَ$seed$, $seed$[It is] the Day they will be tormented over the Fire$seed$),
  (51, 15, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$إِنَّ ٱلْمُتَّقِينَ فِى جَنَّٰتٍۢ وَعُيُونٍ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, the righteous will be among gardens and springs,$seed$),
  (51, 17, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$كَانُوا۟ قَلِيلًۭا مِّنَ ٱلَّيْلِ مَا يَهْجَعُونَ$seed$, $seed$They used to sleep but little of the night,$seed$),
  (51, 18, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$وَبِٱلْأَسْحَارِ هُمْ يَسْتَغْفِرُونَ$seed$, $seed$And in the hours before dawn they would ask forgiveness,$seed$),
  (51, 19, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$وَفِىٓ أَمْوَٰلِهِمْ حَقٌّۭ لِّلسَّآئِلِ وَٱلْمَحْرُومِ$seed$, $seed$And from their properties was [given] the right of the [needy] petitioner and the deprived.$seed$),
  (51, 20, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$وَفِى ٱلْأَرْضِ ءَايَٰتٌۭ لِّلْمُوقِنِينَ$seed$, $seed$And on the earth are signs for the certain [in faith]$seed$),
  (51, 21, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$وَفِىٓ أَنفُسِكُمْ ۚ أَفَلَا تُبْصِرُونَ$seed$, $seed$And in yourselves. Then will you not see?$seed$),
  (51, 22, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$وَفِى ٱلسَّمَآءِ رِزْقُكُمْ وَمَا تُوعَدُونَ$seed$, $seed$And in the heaven is your provision and whatever you are promised.$seed$),
  (51, 26, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$فَرَاغَ إِلَىٰٓ أَهْلِهِۦ فَجَآءَ بِعِجْلٍۢ سَمِينٍۢ$seed$, $seed$Then he went to his family and came with a fat [roasted] calf$seed$),
  (51, 27, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$فَقَرَّبَهُۥٓ إِلَيْهِمْ قَالَ أَلَا تَأْكُلُونَ$seed$, $seed$And placed it near them; he said, "Will you not eat?"$seed$),
  (51, 31, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$۞ قَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكُمْ أَيُّهَا ٱلْمُرْسَلُونَ$seed$, $seed$[Abraham] said, "Then what is your business [here], O messengers?"$seed$),
  (51, 33, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$لِنُرْسِلَ عَلَيْهِمْ حِجَارَةًۭ مِّن طِينٍۢ$seed$, $seed$To send down upon them stones of clay,$seed$),
  (51, 34, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$مُّسَوَّمَةً عِندَ رَبِّكَ لِلْمُسْرِفِينَ$seed$, $seed$Marked in the presence of your Lord for the transgressors."$seed$),
  (51, 48, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$وَٱلْأَرْضَ فَرَشْنَٰهَا فَنِعْمَ ٱلْمَٰهِدُونَ$seed$, $seed$And the earth We have spread out, and excellent is the preparer.$seed$),
  (51, 53, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$أَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِهِۦ ۚ بَلْ هُمْ قَوْمٌۭ طَاغُونَ$seed$, $seed$Did they suggest it to them? Rather, they [themselves] are a transgressing people.$seed$),
  (51, 54, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$فَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ فَمَآ أَنتَ بِمَلُومٍۢ$seed$, $seed$So leave them, [O Muhammad], for you are not to be blamed.$seed$),
  (51, 55, $seed$Adh-Dhaariyat$seed$, $seed$وَذَكِّرْ فَإِنَّ ٱلذِّكْرَىٰ تَنفَعُ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ$seed$, $seed$And remind, for indeed, the reminder benefits the believers.$seed$),
  (52, 1, $seed$At-Tur$seed$, $seed$وَٱلطُّورِ$seed$, $seed$By the mount$seed$),
