  (52, 5, $seed$At-Tur$seed$, $seed$وَٱلسَّقْفِ ٱلْمَرْفُوعِ$seed$, $seed$And [by] the heaven raised high$seed$),
  (52, 6, $seed$At-Tur$seed$, $seed$وَٱلْبَحْرِ ٱلْمَسْجُورِ$seed$, $seed$And [by] the sea filled [with fire],$seed$),
  (52, 7, $seed$At-Tur$seed$, $seed$إِنَّ عَذَابَ رَبِّكَ لَوَٰقِعٌۭ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, the punishment of your Lord will occur.$seed$),
  (52, 8, $seed$At-Tur$seed$, $seed$مَّا لَهُۥ مِن دَافِعٍۢ$seed$, $seed$Of it there is no preventer.$seed$),
  (52, 9, $seed$At-Tur$seed$, $seed$يَوْمَ تَمُورُ ٱلسَّمَآءُ مَوْرًۭا$seed$, $seed$On the Day the heaven will sway with circular motion$seed$),
  (52, 10, $seed$At-Tur$seed$, $seed$وَتَسِيرُ ٱلْجِبَالُ سَيْرًۭا$seed$, $seed$And the mountains will pass on, departing -$seed$),
  (52, 11, $seed$At-Tur$seed$, $seed$فَوَيْلٌۭ يَوْمَئِذٍۢ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِينَ$seed$, $seed$Then woe, that Day, to the deniers,$seed$),
  (52, 12, $seed$At-Tur$seed$, $seed$ٱلَّذِينَ هُمْ فِى خَوْضٍۢ يَلْعَبُونَ$seed$, $seed$Who are in [empty] discourse amusing themselves.$seed$),
  (52, 13, $seed$At-Tur$seed$, $seed$يَوْمَ يُدَعُّونَ إِلَىٰ نَارِ جَهَنَّمَ دَعًّا$seed$, $seed$The Day they are thrust toward the fire of Hell with a [violent] thrust, [its angels will say],$seed$),
  (52, 15, $seed$At-Tur$seed$, $seed$أَفَسِحْرٌ هَٰذَآ أَمْ أَنتُمْ لَا تُبْصِرُونَ$seed$, $seed$Then is this magic, or do you not see?$seed$),
  (52, 17, $seed$At-Tur$seed$, $seed$إِنَّ ٱلْمُتَّقِينَ فِى جَنَّٰتٍۢ وَنَعِيمٍۢ$seed$, $seed$Indeed, the righteous will be in gardens and pleasure,$seed$),
  (52, 25, $seed$At-Tur$seed$, $seed$وَأَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍۢ يَتَسَآءَلُونَ$seed$, $seed$And they will approach one another, inquiring of each other.$seed$),
  (52, 39, $seed$At-Tur$seed$, $seed$أَمْ لَهُ ٱلْبَنَٰتُ وَلَكُمُ ٱلْبَنُونَ$seed$, $seed$Or has He daughters while you have sons?$seed$),
  (52, 41, $seed$At-Tur$seed$, $seed$أَمْ عِندَهُمُ ٱلْغَيْبُ فَهُمْ يَكْتُبُونَ$seed$, $seed$Or have they [knowledge of] the unseen, so they write [it] down?$seed$),
  (52, 49, $seed$At-Tur$seed$, $seed$وَمِنَ ٱلَّيْلِ فَسَبِّحْهُ وَإِدْبَٰرَ ٱلنُّجُومِ$seed$, $seed$And in a part of the night exalt Him and after [the setting of] the stars.$seed$),
  (53, 1, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$وَٱلنَّجْمِ إِذَا هَوَىٰ$seed$, $seed$By the star when it descends,$seed$),
  (53, 2, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$مَا ضَلَّ صَاحِبُكُمْ وَمَا غَوَىٰ$seed$, $seed$Your companion [Muhammad] has not strayed, nor has he erred,$seed$),
  (53, 3, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$وَمَا يَنطِقُ عَنِ ٱلْهَوَىٰٓ$seed$, $seed$Nor does he speak from [his own] inclination.$seed$),
  (53, 4, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$إِنْ هُوَ إِلَّا وَحْىٌۭ يُوحَىٰ$seed$, $seed$It is not but a revelation revealed,$seed$),
  (53, 5, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$عَلَّمَهُۥ شَدِيدُ ٱلْقُوَىٰ$seed$, $seed$Taught to him by one intense in strength -$seed$),
  (53, 6, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$ذُو مِرَّةٍۢ فَٱسْتَوَىٰ$seed$, $seed$One of soundness. And he rose to [his] true form$seed$),
  (53, 7, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$وَهُوَ بِٱلْأُفُقِ ٱلْأَعْلَىٰ$seed$, $seed$While he was in the higher [part of the] horizon.$seed$),
  (53, 8, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$ثُمَّ دَنَا فَتَدَلَّىٰ$seed$, $seed$Then he approached and descended$seed$),
  (53, 9, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$فَكَانَ قَابَ قَوْسَيْنِ أَوْ أَدْنَىٰ$seed$, $seed$And was at a distance of two bow lengths or nearer.$seed$),
  (53, 10, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$فَأَوْحَىٰٓ إِلَىٰ عَبْدِهِۦ مَآ أَوْحَىٰ$seed$, $seed$And he revealed to His Servant what he revealed.$seed$),
  (53, 11, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$مَا كَذَبَ ٱلْفُؤَادُ مَا رَأَىٰٓ$seed$, $seed$The heart did not lie [about] what it saw.$seed$),
  (53, 12, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$أَفَتُمَٰرُونَهُۥ عَلَىٰ مَا يَرَىٰ$seed$, $seed$So will you dispute with him over what he saw?$seed$),
  (53, 13, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$وَلَقَدْ رَءَاهُ نَزْلَةً أُخْرَىٰ$seed$, $seed$And he certainly saw him in another descent$seed$),
  (53, 14, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$عِندَ سِدْرَةِ ٱلْمُنتَهَىٰ$seed$, $seed$At the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary -$seed$),
  (53, 15, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$عِندَهَا جَنَّةُ ٱلْمَأْوَىٰٓ$seed$, $seed$Near it is the Garden of Refuge -$seed$),
  (53, 16, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$إِذْ يَغْشَى ٱلسِّدْرَةَ مَا يَغْشَىٰ$seed$, $seed$When there covered the Lote Tree that which covered [it].$seed$),
  (53, 17, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$مَا زَاغَ ٱلْبَصَرُ وَمَا طَغَىٰ$seed$, $seed$The sight [of the Prophet] did not swerve, nor did it transgress [its limit].$seed$),
  (53, 18, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$لَقَدْ رَأَىٰ مِنْ ءَايَٰتِ رَبِّهِ ٱلْكُبْرَىٰٓ$seed$, $seed$He certainly saw of the greatest signs of his Lord.$seed$),
  (53, 19, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$أَفَرَءَيْتُمُ ٱللَّٰتَ وَٱلْعُزَّىٰ$seed$, $seed$So have you considered al-Lat and al-'Uzza?$seed$),
  (53, 20, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$وَمَنَوٰةَ ٱلثَّالِثَةَ ٱلْأُخْرَىٰٓ$seed$, $seed$And Manat, the third - the other one?$seed$),
  (53, 21, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$أَلَكُمُ ٱلذَّكَرُ وَلَهُ ٱلْأُنثَىٰ$seed$, $seed$Is the male for you and for Him the female?$seed$),
  (53, 22, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$تِلْكَ إِذًۭا قِسْمَةٌۭ ضِيزَىٰٓ$seed$, $seed$That, then, is an unjust division.$seed$),
  (53, 24, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$أَمْ لِلْإِنسَٰنِ مَا تَمَنَّىٰ$seed$, $seed$Or is there for man whatever he wishes?$seed$),
  (53, 25, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$فَلِلَّهِ ٱلْءَاخِرَةُ وَٱلْأُولَىٰ$seed$, $seed$Rather, to Allah belongs the Hereafter and the first [life].$seed$),
  (53, 33, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$أَفَرَءَيْتَ ٱلَّذِى تَوَلَّىٰ$seed$, $seed$Have you seen the one who turned away$seed$),
  (53, 34, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$وَأَعْطَىٰ قَلِيلًۭا وَأَكْدَىٰٓ$seed$, $seed$And gave a little and [then] refrained?$seed$),
  (53, 35, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$أَعِندَهُۥ عِلْمُ ٱلْغَيْبِ فَهُوَ يَرَىٰٓ$seed$, $seed$Does he have knowledge of the unseen, so he sees?$seed$),
  (53, 36, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$أَمْ لَمْ يُنَبَّأْ بِمَا فِى صُحُفِ مُوسَىٰ$seed$, $seed$Or has he not been informed of what was in the scriptures of Moses$seed$),
  (53, 37, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$وَإِبْرَٰهِيمَ ٱلَّذِى وَفَّىٰٓ$seed$, $seed$And [of] Abraham, who fulfilled [his obligations] -$seed$),
  (53, 38, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$أَلَّا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌۭ وِزْرَ أُخْرَىٰ$seed$, $seed$That no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another$seed$),
  (53, 39, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$وَأَن لَّيْسَ لِلْإِنسَٰنِ إِلَّا مَا سَعَىٰ$seed$, $seed$And that there is not for man except that [good] for which he strives$seed$),
  (53, 40, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$وَأَنَّ سَعْيَهُۥ سَوْفَ يُرَىٰ$seed$, $seed$And that his effort is going to be seen -$seed$),
  (53, 41, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$ثُمَّ يُجْزَىٰهُ ٱلْجَزَآءَ ٱلْأَوْفَىٰ$seed$, $seed$Then he will be recompensed for it with the fullest recompense$seed$),
  (53, 42, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$وَأَنَّ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكَ ٱلْمُنتَهَىٰ$seed$, $seed$And that to your Lord is the finality$seed$),
  (53, 43, $seed$An-Najm$seed$, $seed$وَأَنَّهُۥ هُوَ أَضْحَكَ وَأَبْكَىٰ$seed$, $seed$And that it is He who makes [one] laugh and weep$seed$),
